<title>UK: Cadbury shares up on Coke price rise report.</title>
<headline>Cadbury shares up on Coke price rise report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British food and drinks group Cadbury Schweppes Plc climbed on Thursday after the Wall Street Journal said Coca-Cola Co might increase prices after July 4, potentially ending the price war in the U.S. soft drink industry.</p>
<p>&quot;That should be good for Cadbury's if it puts an end to the price war,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Cadbury, which owns U.S. soft drink group Dr Pepper/Seven-Up, was 7-1/2p firmer at 533-1/2 by 0844 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
